      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#1 · the Genesis retelling in the consulted Layton telling",
          "title": "A formed human exceeds the makers",
          "italic": "The scene demonstrates the distinction between forming, naming and governing within a field, and originating the life that exceeds the jurisdiction claimed over it.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The tractate retells Genesis through its own exegesis. The rulers participate in forming Adam after an image they have perceived; the human becomes living through a power they do not finally own — breath fails until spirit descends from the Adamantine Land. Animals receive names; the garden brings prohibition; sleep becomes ignorance. The spiritual woman awakens Adam and escapes pursuit as a tree, leaving a shadow that the rulers sexually violate; the",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "instructing principle enters and leaves the serpent; eating exposes spiritual nakedness; fig leaves, blame, curses, expulsion and imposed toil follow. Formation and pursuit belong together: inability to originate the life they seek is followed by attempt to possess its manifestation. The distinction between the woman and the shadow is materially necessary to Norea's later denial of their claimed genealogy — the violated figure is not made to disappear from the narrative.\n\nOccurrences: the formed Adam and the descending spirit (#1); the tree-escape (#1); the violated shadow (#1, grounding #2); the garden, sleep and expulsion (#1).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
