      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#2 · the flood and the refusal (q004's scope in the source house)",
          "title": "Norea refuses the ancestry of possession",
          "italic": "Her refusal demonstrates the contest at the level of origin: the rulers' claim to rule is contested not by stronger force but by recovered genealogy.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "Cain farms; Abel keeps sheep; rejected and accepted offerings lead to fratricide, accusing blood and sevenfold vengeance. Seth follows; Eve bears Norea. A ruler warns Noah of the flood; the ark rests on Mount Sir; Noah excludes Norea, whose breath burns the ark, and he rebuilds. When the rulers later claim authority over her through Eve, Norea refuses the genealogy they impose: she is not their descendant and comes from the world above. Their claim to rule is contested at the level of origin. They attempt coercion; Norea cries to the higher divine reality for rescue.",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.55,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 620
        },
        {
