      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#3 · the retrospective cosmology through Eleleth's revelation (q005's scope)",
          "title": "Eleleth: rescue and the rulers' own origin",
          "italic": "The revelation demonstrates the decisive operation: authority limited by recovered provenance — Norea receives an account of where the rulers came from, after they presumed to say where she came from.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "Eleleth, one of the great luminaries, descends: he rescues Norea from the rulers' immediate claim and teaches her about her root and their own origin. Pistis Sophia desired to create without her consort; a veil lies between the world above and the lower realms; shadow comes into being beneath the veil and becomes matter; a deficient, arrogant lion-like ruler emerges and, opening his eyes on apparently limitless matter, repeats the totalising claim. Sophia introduces light into matter, exposing the mistake without making the lower realm unreal. The ruler generates",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "seven offspring; rule distributes through layered heavens and chaotic realms, Sabaoth placed in the seventh heaven beneath the veil. Zoe, daughter of Pistis Sophia, rebukes the arrogant ruler; her breath becomes a fiery angel binding Yaldabaoth in Tartaros. Sabaoth sees the higher power, rejects his father and matter, praises Sophia and Zoe, and is elevated in the seventh heaven — recognition within structure, not only escape from it. The two rebellions keep distinct offices: Sabaoth changes allegiance inside the genealogy; Norea denies the genealogy contains her root.\n\nOccurrences: Eleleth's descent, appearance and teaching (#2–#3); the veil, shadow and matter (#3, compared at #4); the seven offspring and layered heavens (#3); Zoe's rebuke and Sabaoth's repentance (#3).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
