      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#4–#5→0 · the ending's bounded synopsis (Robinson); the Native 020 seam now owned; the human-amplified ledger",
          "title": "The root disclosed; the ending still to come",
          "italic": "The story's rulers are most dangerous not because they are unreal but because real local power is mistaken for self-grounding total authority — a system synthesis, human-amplified: no until ratified.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "Eleleth's revelation promises disclosure after three generations: the true Man will bring saving disclosure, spiritual beings freed, the authorities' world losing dominion; the closing hymn gives the ending a collective voice before Father, Son and Holy Spirit. Norea's immediate rescue is not narrated as the completion of the cosmic history. The whole's deepest source-side movement is false sovereignty corrected by provenance: the rulers' local world is not imaginary — they possess real efficacy inside it — but their mistake is inferring from local efficacy and visibility",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "that their order is self-grounding and exhaustive. The layered-cosmos seam now has an intact owner. Four system candidates stay human-amplified: no — the chief ruler's Hybris figuration; the veil/Māyā comparison with its different metaphysical valences; the archon/technical-evaluator image; and the Norea comparisons with Number Six and Daphne, whose historical, gendered and religious specificity must remain primary. The Neumann comparison stays a proposal, not a renaming of Norea as hero; the Valentinian whole remains distinct — Horos and Achamoth are not inserted here.\n\nDeclared cross-story: distinct from the Valentinian Sophia–Horos–Achamoth whole; no transmission asserted across the shared Sophia name. ↳ Occurrences: the refusal and the disclosure (#2–#3, #5→0); the promised ending (#4, #5→0).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
